---
// Safe to edit by hand
// scaffold-file: church
// The Visitor on the home page (2026-09-24, feat/the-visitor): one slim band,
// "The Visitor · September 2026 issue · Read it", with the issue's small cover.
//
// NOT A PAGE-BUILDER BLOCK, like "Last Sunday": the home page is composed in
// Sanity and adding a block there is a content write, so the band is drawn from
// code and placed through SectionRenderer's `insert` slot, straight after Last
// Sunday and before the Church Blog rows (src/pages/index.astro).
//
// EVERYTHING IS DERIVED (rule 15). The issue is the newest on the /visitor
// page, read by the build step (scripts/visitor-covers.mjs) into
// src/data/visitor.generated.json; the band updates itself the build after an
// editor adds an issue. It renders only once that page is published (before,
// there is nothing for it to point at), and in the Playwright build from the
// committed fixture.
//
// IT LINKS TO /visitor, NOT TO THE PDF. The issues are 15 to 75 MB files; a
// tap on the home page of a phone should not start one unannounced. /visitor
// opens on the same issue, large, with its size beside the button, so the
// newest issue is still one tap from the band and a second from the file,
// and the archive is right under it.
//
// The ground is paper, between the indigo of Last Sunday above and the taupe
// of the blog rows below, and it matches neither. The whole row is one link;
// its words name it, so the cover inside it is decorative.
import IssueCover from '@/components/visitor/IssueCover.astro';
import { NEWSLETTER, coverFor, type Issue, type CoverInfo } from '@/lib/visitor-issues';

interface Props {
  issue: Issue;
  covers: Record<string, CoverInfo>;
  href: string;
}

const { issue, covers, href } = Astro.props as Props;
---

<section
  class="vb-band border-y border-indigo/10 bg-bg text-indigo"
  aria-label={NEWSLETTER}
  data-visitor-band={issue.anchor}
  data-pagefind-ignore
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,40px)]">
    <a {href} class="vb-link group">
      <span class="vb-cover">
        <IssueCover issue={issue} cover={coverFor(issue, covers)} sizes="80px" decorative />
      </span>
      <span class="vb-words">
        <span class="vb-name">{NEWSLETTER}</span>
        <span class="vb-dot" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span class="vb-issue">{issue.label} issue</span>
        <span class="vb-dot" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span class="vb-read">
          Read it<span
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="ml-2 inline-block transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1 group-focus-visible:translate-x-1"
            >&#8594;</span
          >
        </span>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .vb-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(16px, 3vw, 32px);
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .vb-link:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-indigo);
    outline-offset: 6px;
  }
  .vb-cover {
    flex: none;
    width: clamp(56px, 8vw, 80px);
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-indigo) 18%, transparent),
      0 8px 18px -12px rgb(28 27 58 / 0.5);
  }
  .vb-words {
    display: flex;
    min-width: 0;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    column-gap: 0.75rem;
    row-gap: 0.25rem;
  }
  .vb-name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.4vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-indigo);
  }
  .vb-issue {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.8vw, 1.3125rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .vb-dot {
    color: var(--color-gold-ink);
  }
  .vb-read {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: var(--text-ui);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-eyebrow);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-gold-ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
    padding-bottom: 2px;
  }
  /* On a phone the three parts stack under the name, so the dots go. */
  @media (max-width: 639.98px) {
    .vb-words {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
    .vb-dot {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
